For cargo carrier: insurance premium = [(valuation + fuel capacity) * number of risky zones + inflammable material quantity] / (number of passenger *1000).

Design a C++ program that can simulate above scenario. Ensure that you use a computeInsurance() method to display the insurance premium and implement it in such a way so that it become mandatory to define it in all the cruise and cargo classes.
[CO2(Creating), 4M]

Q4. Do not consider syntax errors.

(a) Predict the output and modify the program so that it can print "Dino cannot be zero." "Memory was allocated successfully but dino was zero!!". [CO4(Analyzing), 3M]

```cpp
#include<iostream>
using namespace std;
class Fraction
{ int num, dino;
public:
Fraction(){}
void setFraction(int n, int d){
if(d==0)
throw" Dino cannot be zero.";
else
num=n;
dino=d;
}};
int main()
{
int size=1, a=5, b=0;
Fraction *arr;
cin>>size;
arr = new Fraction[size];
try{
if(arr==NULL)
throw" Memory Error";
else{
for (int i=0; i<size; i++)
{
try{
arr[i].setFraction(a, b);
}
catch(const char * s){
cout<<s<<endl;
throw s;
}}}
catch(const char *s) {
cout<<s<<endl;
}
return 0;}
```

